# The charter § 2.1 byte-integrity law: the A5 axis's payload is BYTES, and
# seeds are asserted LF-only by expand.py's parser - git must never rewrite
# them at checkout on any machine.
seeds/** -text
controls/** -text
expectations/** -text
*.tsv -text
# The instruments themselves stay LF (the cq review's SF-8: a CRLF checkout
# of the .sh breaks WSL bash - the repo's own recorded lesson; .py LF keeps
# the committed digests meaningful).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
